  "content": {
    "title": "Matt Painter glad 'burden toward Purdue' basketball is over, focuses on getting back to Final Four",
    "text": "March 25, 2026, 6:59 p.m. ETPurdue coach Matt Painter once held the title of \"best coach yet to make a Final Four.\"Painter said the label did not bother him personally but motivated him to achieve the milestone for Purdue.The Boilermakers' 2024 national championship game appearance was the program's first Final Four in 44 years.SAN JOSE, CA — Purdue basketball coach Matt Painter once wore the backhanded compliment of \"best coach yet to make a Final Four.\"The West Region semifinals potentially put the Boilermakers in the path of a couple of the coaches wearing that label. One is Sean Miller, who leads Texas against Purdue in Thursday's Sweet 16 game. The other is Arizona's Tommy Lloyd, who faces another accomplished coach — Arkansas' John Calipari — in the other semifinal.Painter said that Final Four absence did not bother him as a reflection of his personal accomplishments. It was, however, a motivator to break through for his school. The Boilermakers' run to the national championship game in 2024 was the program's first Final Four trip in 44 years.\"I didn't look at it as a burden personally. I looked at it as a burden toward Purdue,\" Painter said. \"I didn't like it.\"If you're in the position as a head coach at a high-major school and it bothers you when people say stuff, you're going to be in a tailspin for a while. But I didn't like them saying it about my school. That affects you.\"Buy thisi Purdue Big Ten title page print!Arizona has not made a Final Four since Lute Olson's national championship in 1997. Texas last made a Final Four in 2003 under Rick Barnes.Miller's Xavier team beat Purdue in the second round in 2008 en route to the Elite Eight. He took Arizona there in his second season, 2011, but lost to eventual national champion UConn. The Wildcats went back to regional semifinals in 2014 and '15, but lost to Bo Ryan's Wisconsin teams in both years.Lloyd, who succeeded Miller at Arizona, has taken the Wildcats to three Sweet 16s in four years but has yet to win a semifinal game. In the other season, they were a 2-seed upset victim to 15-seed Yale. That would have been the biggest upset of the tournament, except 16 seed Fairleigh Dickinson beat 1 seed Purdue the next night.Painter, who lost in overtime to eventual national champion Virginia in a 2018 semifinal, can identify with every version of those near-miss experiences.Three of the starters who helped Painter break that Final Four drought — Braden Smith, Fletcher Loyer and Trey Kaufman-Renn — now lead this Purdue team. When Painter talks about motivation now, he again skips past the distinction of potentially becoming the first Boiler coach to make two Final Fours.\"I think when you get to that point, everybody is just trying to help their team, but more than anything for us, we're just trying to help our seniors,\" Painter said. \"We have three seniors that have been together in their careers and they've tied for the all-time winningest players in school history. If they get one more win in the NCAA Tournament, it's the most wins ever by a group in the NCAA Tournament by a group. Those are the type of things that you want.\"We're not in position to go to the Final Four right now. We have to beat Texas to be in that position.\"Nathan Baird and Sam King have the best Purdue sports coverage, and sign up for IndyStar's Boilermakers newsletter.",
    "word_count": 580,
    "extraction_method": "readability"
  },
